# Working rules

- Use targeted edits; never rewrite a whole file for a small change.
- Read only the files named in the task. Do not open docs/design/audit.md,
  docs/backend-findings.md or docs/inventory.md unless the task says so.
- Do not edit docs/design unless the task says so.
- Do not browse the web or fetch docs unless asked; use package.json and the repo.
- Keep plans to 10 lines and summaries to 10 lines. Ask questions only if blocked.
- If the same error persists after two attempts, stop and report what you tried.

# Running checks (cost control)

- Never run yarn validate, yarn test or yarn test:e2e; the human runs the full suite.
- After each step run yarn typecheck and yarn test:fast <changed test files>, with
  output capped: append `2>&1 | Select-Object -Last 40`.

# Testing policy

- Test logic, data mapping, privacy (dropped fields), money, auth and guest gating,
  and state derivation. One smoke test per screen (populated, loading, error).
- No per-variant or per-prop tests for presentational components, and no tests
  that only restate the implementation.
- Test behavior, not implementation. Query by role, label or text, never testID.
  No whole-screen snapshots. No `any`.
- Network calls use typed MSW handlers (types from the Zod schemas via z.infer).
- Every bug fix ships with a regression test; a test must fail if the feature it
  covers is broken.
- New source folders go into collectCoverageFrom in jest.config.js in the same PR.

# App rules

- Every route sets a unique document title: "Page | Kikae" (dynamic pages from
  their data).
- Schemas declare only the fields the app uses; never log or store tokens or other
  private fields.
- Tokens only: no hex colors, no arbitrary Tailwind values; all text goes through
  the Text component.
- Routes outside the tabs use the shared screen wrapper and respect safe-area insets.
